# Local state and secrets. NEVER commit these.
#
# A Netscape cookies.txt is a live, unexpirable Google session: possession is
# account takeover across every Google service sharing those cookies. The
# engine auto-discovers `./cookies.txt` from the working directory
# (Final/cookie_providers.py), and the docs show `--cookies` with a relative
# path, so a contributor following them lands one in the working tree. In a
# public repository one `git add -A` in a fork publishes it, and git history
# keeps it reachable long after the file is deleted.
cookies.txt
*cookies*.txt
active.txt
active_backup.txt
webui.txt
webui.url
queue.json
history.jsonl
config.toml
!Final/examples/config.example.toml
.venv/
Final/test_outputs/
*.rar
.superpowers/
.worktrees/
